@id n4_choirc
# DRAFT
# Brother Piers on the east walk at dusk (night 4, fog). Background; dry.
# What the brothers say: the abbot's visitor, and the fast to starve it. If Thomas has named Simon (n4_thomas_simon):
# Thomas nursed Simon through a fever at Michaelmas, and Simon would do anything Thomas told him.
== start
(Brother Piers on the east walk, watching the fog fill the garth like milk in a bowl.)
Piers {wary}: You can't see the far walk. I keep thinking someone's standing in it.
-> topics

== again
Piers {calm}: Still foggy.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_choirc_talk] What are the brothers saying? -> talk
* [if n4_thomas_simon] [if not n4_choirc_simon] What do you know of Brother Simon? -> simon

== talk [set n4_choirc_talk]
Piers {grave}: That the abbot saw it at the foot of his bed. That it's hungry, and we fast so it finds nothing in us to eat.
(He doesn't smile.)
Piers {grave}: I'd sooner eat.
-> topics

== simon [set n4_choirc_simon]
Piers {calm}: Simon keeps to himself. Thomas nursed him through a fever at Michaelmas, and he's been Thomas's shadow since.
Piers {grave}: He'd walk into the river if Thomas told him it was good for his chest.
-> topics

== leave
Piers {wary}: Mind the fog, porter.
